                <pb facs="0693" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.796 Pan American Airways, Inc./413:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-06T19:00:00-04:00">May 6, 1929—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>48. Post Office Department requests that you be advised for information of
                    Chilean Government that the Attorney General has approved <pb facs="0694"
                        n="558" xml:id="pg558"/> the contract awarded to the Pan American-Grace
                    Airways for transporting mails south from Panama Canal to Chile, and that the
                    contract is in effect and operations will begin immediately as far as Mollendo
                    and will be extended to Chile as soon as necessary arrangement is made with the
                    Chilean Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
